const vogueReading=`<div class="magazine-reading"><div class="magazine-tag">VOGUE · ADAPTED CLASSROOM READING</div>${image('fashion','Street style fashion and a personalised feed','tall')}<div class="magazine-copy"><h3>What Does Your TikTok Algorithm Say About You?</h3><p class="article-byline">Based on Sarah Spellings’ article in <i>Vogue</i>, 22 December 2021. This is an original, simplified retelling for language practice, not the original article.</p><div class="story-text"><p>Open your TikTok For You Page and you might see a beauty tutorial, a celebrity interview or an extremely niche video about something you never knew existed. Your friend could open the same app and see something completely different. The algorithm doesn’t just recommend popular posts: it curates a personalised feed from signals such as the videos you watch, like and comment on.</p><p>Watch time matters. If you get hooked on a clip and watch it until the end, the app may recommend more content like it. Even when you don’t follow a creator, their videos can keep popping up on your FYP. Sometimes, the algorithm also introduces unexpected posts so that you don’t get bored scrolling through the same topics.</p><p>But does your FYP show your real personality? Not necessarily. Watching a celebrity’s interviews doesn’t mean you want to live their life. You might watch a video about a stranger’s daily routine simply because it is interesting. Or you might scroll through fashion posts for work while preferring comedy in your free time.</p><p>The writer describes how her FYP includes some predictable interests, like music and celebrity gossip, alongside surprising lifestyle videos. Her feed feels personal, yet it doesn’t tell the whole story. The same is true for Sasha, who usually follows makeup artists but is watching more interviews with Jacob Elordi these days. Meanwhile, Kirill thinks his FYP understands him perfectly; Kristina believes it is sometimes completely wrong.</p><p>Perhaps your FYP is not a personality test after all. It is a changing picture of what holds your attention, and it may reveal your curiosity as much as your identity.</p></div><a href="https://www.vogue.com/article/tiktok-algorithm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-btn">↗ Read the original Vogue article</a></div></div>`;
